 "derivations": [
  {
   "id": "transport",
   "what": "the solution $u(x,t) = f(x - \\alpha t)$ of the transport equation",
   "source": "Notes on Diffy Qs, 1.9 First-order linear PDEs, the transport equation of Example 1.9.1 worked in characteristic coordinates",
   "nodes": [
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "tex": "\\xi = x - \\alpha t , \\qquad s = t",
       "src": "Example 1.9.1"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{ux}{\\kux} = \\mk{a}{\\kuxi}\\,\\mk{ax}{\\xi_x} + \\mk{b}{\\kus}\\,\\mk{bx}{s_x}",
      "src": "Calculus, 14.5",
      "why": "The chain rule in several variables, with $u$ a function of $\\xi$ and $s$, which are functions of $x$ and $t$."
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ux}{\\kux} = \\mk{a}{\\kuxi}\\,\\mk{ax}{\\cdot 1} + \\mk{b}{\\kus}\\,\\mk{bx}{\\cdot 0}",
       "uses": [
        0
       ]
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ux}{\\kux} = \\mk{a}{\\kuxi}",
       "uses": []
      }
     ],
     "src": "Example 1.9.1"
    },
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "tex": "\\xi = x - \\alpha t , \\qquad s = t",
       "src": "Example 1.9.1"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kut} = \\mk{a}{\\kuxi}\\,\\mk{ax}{\\xi_t} + \\mk{b}{\\kus}\\,\\mk{bx}{s_t}",
      "src": "Calculus, 14.5",
      "why": "The chain rule again, now differentiating in $t$."
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kut} = \\mk{a}{\\kuxi}\\,\\mk{ax}{\\cdot(-\\alpha)} + \\mk{b}{\\kus}\\,\\mk{bx}{\\cdot 1}",
       "uses": [
        0
       ]
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kut} = \\mk{ax}{-\\alpha}\\,\\mk{a}{\\kuxi} + \\mk{b}{\\kus}",
       "uses": []
      }
     ],
     "src": "Example 1.9.1"
    },
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "step": 0
      },
      {
       "step": 1
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{al}{\\alpha}\\,\\mk{ux}{\\kux} + \\mk{ut}{\\kut} = \\mk{z}{0}",
      "src": "Example 1.9.1"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{al}{\\alpha}\\,\\mk{ux}{\\underbrace{(\\kuxi)}_{\\kux}} + \\mk{ut}{\\underbrace{(- \\alpha \\kuxi + \\kus)}_{\\kut}} = \\mk{z}{0}",
       "uses": [
        0,
        1
       ]
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kus} = \\mk{z}{0}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "The two terms $\\alpha u_\\xi$ and $-\\alpha u_\\xi$ cancel."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kduds} = \\mk{z}{0}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "Treating $\\xi$ as simply a parameter, we have obtained the ODE $\\frac{du}{ds} = 0$. That is trivial to solve."
      }
     ],
     "src": "Example 1.9.1"
    },
    {
     "assumes": [
      {
       "step": 2
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\xi = x - \\alpha t , \\qquad s = t",
       "src": "Example 1.9.1"
      }
     ],
     "then": {
      "tex": "\\mk{ut}{\\kduds} = \\mk{z}{0}",
      "src": "Example 1.9.1"
     },
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{u}{\\ku} = \\mk{A}{A(\\xi)}",
       "uses": [],
       "cap": "The solution is a function that does not depend on $s$ (but it does depend on $\\xi$). That is, there is some function $A$ such that $u = A(\\xi)$."
      },
      {
       "tex": "\\mk{u}{\\ku} = \\mk{A}{A(x - \\alpha t)}",
       "uses": [
        1
